<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Norddeutscher Lloyd</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1857">1857</a>–<a href="/years/1970">1970</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as North German Lloyd</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Norddeutscher Lloyd was a shipping company founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a> in 1857. Operating from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremerhaven">Bremerhaven</a>, it carried millions of emigrants to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and became one of the largest shipping companies in the world, winning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-riband">Blue Riband</a> with liners such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ss-kaiser-wilhelm-der-grosse">Kaiser Wilhelm der Grosse</a> and the Bremen. In 1970 it merged with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg-america-line">Hamburg America Line</a> to form Hapag-Lloyd.</p></div>
